This is a derivative work: the C extension vendors the original
algorithm C sources (isotope.c, element.c, parse.c, peak.c, profile.c,
combination.c) unmodified, and `iso_core.c`/`iso_core.h` are extracted
directly from the original `main.c` as a structural (non-algorithmic)
refactor. The Python layer re-implements the R package's pipeline
functions from scratch, reproducing their documented numeric behavior;
any intentional deviations from R's behavior (bug fixes, pythonic API
changes) are disclosed in the corresponding merge request descriptions,
not silently introduced. See AUTHORS for full attribution.
